---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-26-pedigrees-and-client-portal.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-26',
  title: 'Refreshed workflow pages: Pedigrees and Client Portal',
  tags: ['workflows', 'pedigrees', 'client-portal', 'seo'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 26, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Refreshed the Pedigrees and Client Portal workflow pages to match what the product now does, and
    corrected the genetics wording on the Pedigrees page.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Pages updated</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><a href="/workflows/pedigrees" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/pedigrees</a>: new sections on exporting a pedigree as a PDF and sharing it by PIN-protected link (72 hours, revocable), recorded ancestors (fill a slot, edit, link, merge, remove), and COI with common ancestors, including when a figure is withheld as Not Enough Pedigree. Links to record import and Bring What You Already Have. The lethal-gene line now says the check screens both parents' recorded results against a curated list, and that no warning is not a clearance.</li>
      <li><a href="/workflows/client-portal" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/client-portal</a>: the old contract section is now a short summary linking to <a href="/workflows/contracts-and-e-signatures" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">Contracts &amp; E-Signatures</a>. New sections on how buyers get portal access and invite delivery tracking, and on go-home scheduling (buyers book or you schedule every buyer, the schedule view, buyer emails) and adult animal pickup. Payment copy now matches the invoice help article: card payment when the breeder accepts it, payment instructions otherwise.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Screenshots</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      No new screenshots yet; they follow separately.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
